;; One mutation per invariant. `:find` must occur EXACTLY ONCE in `:file` —
;; `tools/mutate.cljs` refuses otherwise, because a mutation that landed in a
;; comment or in a second call site produces a red suite that proves nothing.
;;
;; Read the pair before trusting a red: the thing broken and the thing
;; reported must be the same thing.
;;
;; ## SCOPE — this table does not cover the whole repository
;;
;; It covers exactly three things:
;;
;;   1. `POST /api/handoff` — the route that brings back what
;;      `cloud-itonami-isco-4311` did with a payroll run this actor emitted,
;;      and the only thing that makes `payroll.handoff` reachable at all.
;;   2. The 源泉徴収 hold's EXPLANATION (rules 5 and 6 of `payroll.governor`),
;;      after taxlaw gained `[:eu]` and `[:us]`.
;;   3. 年末調整 — `payroll.nenmatsu`, the `:assess-year-end-adjustment` rules
;;      in `payroll.governor`, its route, and the two places its records had
;;      to become legible in the ledger (added 2026-08-18).
;;
;; What is NOT covered, and would be measured by nothing if this table were
;; read as a whole-repo verdict: the wage/net arithmetic rules, the advisor,
;; both store backends, `payroll.shiwake`, the pure `payroll.handoff`, and
;; `POST /api/payroll-run`'s own body parsing. All of those have suites; none
;; of those suites has been shown here to be capable of failing. A clean run
;; means "every invariant LISTED BELOW is measured", never "this actor is
;; measured" — reading it as the second would be exactly the defect the
;; harness exists to catch: a check that did not look reporting the same
;; value as one that looked and found nothing.
;;
;; ## Two entries were REMOVED, and why
;;
;; ### `:the-taxlaw-pin-carries-the-two-new-jurisdictions` (removed 2026-08-18)
;;
;; It rolled the `taxlaw` pin back to `a4a68050` and, until 年末調整 landed, it
;; KILLED — the `[:eu]`/`[:us]` withholding tests went red. It now reports
;; **UNMEASURED**: `payroll.nenmatsu` calls `taxlaw/facet-of`, which
;; `a4a68050` does not have, so the rollback breaks the READER and the suite
;; never runs. Per this harness's own rule a mutation that breaks the build
;; demonstrates the build, not an invariant, and must be fixed rather than
;; scored.
;;
;; The property it was measuring did not disappear — it got louder. A stale
;; pin is now caught by the code failing to COMPILE, which is a harder signal
;; than a red test, and the pin's CONTENT is asserted directly by
;; `payroll.nenmatsu-test/a-jurisdiction-whose-year-end-facet-was-not-read-is-refused`,
;; which reads `taxlaw/requires-year-end-adjustment?` for `[:us]` and `[:eu]`
;; out of the dependency itself. `:the-year-end-facet-is-the-one-taxlaw-carries`
;; below measures the same seam from inside this repo, and compiles.
;;
;; ### `:the-ceiling-is-read-from-taxlaw-not-typed`
;;
;; It replaced
;; `(:rule/income-ceiling-yen (taxlaw/facet-of jurisdiction facet))` with the
;; literal `20000000` and SURVIVED — correctly. The only catalogued
;; 年末調整 facet is `[:jp]`, whose ceiling IS 20,000,000, so no test can
;; distinguish the two and none should pretend to. The property is instead
;; measured from the other side by `:the-ceiling-is-actually-read`, which
;; makes the lookup return nil and reddens. Recorded here rather than deleted
;; silently: dropping a mutation to clean a table is the thing this harness
;; exists to prevent, so a drop has to say why.
[{:id :handoff-is-routed
  :invariant "the route exists — without it the reconciliation reaches nothing"
  :file "src/payroll/edge/endpoints.cljc"
  :find "(= path \"/api/handoff\")"
  :replace "(= path \"/api/handoff-disabled\")"}

 {:id :handoff-writes-to-the-ledger
  :invariant "the facts are appended, not merely computed and returned"
  :file "src/payroll/edge/endpoints.cljc"
  :find "(doseq [f facts] (store/append-ledger! store f))"
  :replace "(doseq [f []] (store/append-ledger! store f))"}

 {:id :employer-comes-from-the-did
  :invariant "the body cannot write into another employer's ledger slice"
  :file "src/payroll/edge/endpoints.cljc"
  :find "(assoc (handoff/handoff-fact submission response)\n                                   :client-id client-id)"
  :replace "(merge {:client-id client-id}\n                                   (handoff/handoff-fact submission response))"}

 {:id :a-refused-body-writes-nothing
  :invariant "a 400 appends nothing — half a batch is worse than none"
  :file "src/payroll/edge/endpoints.cljc"
  :find "(if error\n        {:status 400 :body {:ok false :error error}}"
  :replace "(if false\n        {:status 400 :body {:ok false :error error}}"}

 {:id :handoffs-must-be-a-vector
  :invariant "a :handoffs that is not a vector is a 400, not an empty success"
  :file "src/payroll/edge/endpoints.cljc"
  :find "(not (vector? (:handoffs m))) {:error \"body must carry a :handoffs vector\"}"
  :replace "(not (coll? (:handoffs m))) {:error \"body must carry a :handoffs vector\"}"}

 {:id :an-empty-batch-is-refused
  :invariant "an empty :handoffs is a caller error, not a recorded nothing"
  :file "src/payroll/edge/endpoints.cljc"
  :find "(empty? (:handoffs m)) {:error \":handoffs must not be empty\"}"
  :replace "(empty? nil) {:error \":handoffs must not be empty\"}"}

 {:id :each-pair-must-carry-a-submission
  :invariant "a pair with no submission is a 400 before anything is appended"
  :file "src/payroll/edge/endpoints.cljc"
  :find "(not (every? #(map? (:submission %)) (:handoffs m)))"
  :replace "(not (every? #(some? %) (:handoffs m)))"}

 {:id :a-non-map-response-is-the-callers-error
  :invariant "a malformed request is not recorded as an odd answer from 4311"
  :file "src/payroll/edge/endpoints.cljc"
  :find "(not (every? #(map? (:response %)) (:handoffs m)))"
  :replace "(not (every? #(some? %) (:handoffs m)))"}

 {:id :duplicate-is-resolved
  :invariant ":unresolved is what a person must look at; a duplicate is settled"
  :file "src/payroll/edge/endpoints.cljc"
  :find "(contains? #{:posted :duplicate}\n                                                        (:handoff/outcome %))"
  :replace "(contains? #{:posted}\n                                                        (:handoff/outcome %))"}

 {:id :posted-is-resolved
  :invariant "and a success is settled too — :unresolved is not `everything`"
  :file "src/payroll/edge/endpoints.cljc"
  :find "#{:posted :duplicate}\n                                                        (:handoff/outcome %))"
  :replace "#{:duplicate}\n                                                        (:handoff/outcome %))"}

 {:id :handoff-needs-an-allowlist
  :invariant "an unconfigured deployment is 503, not an open write path"
  :file "src/payroll/edge/endpoints.cljc"
  :find "    (nil? allowlist)\n    {:status 503 :body {:ok false :error \"no allow-list configured\"}}\n\n    (nil? (employer-for allowlist caller-did))\n    {:status 403 :body {:ok false :error \"caller not permitted\"}}\n\n    :else\n    (let [{:keys [pairs error]}"
  :replace "    (nil? nil)\n    {:status 503 :body {:ok false :error \"no allow-list configured\"}}\n\n    (nil? (employer-for allowlist caller-did))\n    {:status 403 :body {:ok false :error \"caller not permitted\"}}\n\n    :else\n    (let [{:keys [pairs error]}"

 }

 {:id :handoff-refuses-an-unlisted-caller
  :invariant "an unlisted DID cannot append to anyone's ledger"
  :file "src/payroll/edge/endpoints.cljc"
  :find "    (nil? (employer-for allowlist caller-did))\n    {:status 403 :body {:ok false :error \"caller not permitted\"}}\n\n    :else\n    (let [{:keys [pairs error]}"
  :replace "    (nil? nil)\n    {:status 403 :body {:ok false :error \"caller not permitted\"}}\n\n    :else\n    (let [{:keys [pairs error]}"}

 {:id :a-handoff-is-not-a-commit
  :invariant "a reader counting what this actor paid must not count these"
  :file "src/payroll/handoff.cljc"
  :find "(merge {:disposition :handoff}"
  :replace "(merge {:disposition :commit}"}

 ;; --- two more jurisdictions in taxlaw (2026-08-18). For payroll the risk is
 ;; not that a run gets approved — it does not — but that a HOLD explains
 ;; itself as `unknown country` when the truth is `we did not read IRC §3402`,
 ;; and an operator concludes there is no obligation. ---

 {:id :an-uncheckable-withholding-rule-is-still-a-hold
  :invariant "a US payroll run is held as hard as before the US was catalogued"
  :file "src/payroll/governor.cljc"
  :find "      (= :none (:taxlaw/coverage withholding))"
  :replace "      (= :nope (:taxlaw/coverage withholding))"}

 {:id :the-payroll-hold-explains-itself-accurately
  :invariant "`kotoba.taxlaw に無い` is false for a catalogued jurisdiction"
  :file "src/payroll/governor.cljc"
  :find "             :detail (if-let [why (:taxlaw/why withholding)]"
  :replace "             :detail (if-let [why nil]"}

 {:id :unread-is-not-absent-and-the-detail-says-so
  :invariant "the US does oblige withholding; only the reading is missing"
  :file "src/payroll/governor.cljc"
  :find "                            \"。これは義務が無いという意味ではない\""
  :replace "                            \"。\""}

 {:id :the-out-of-scope-facet-is-forwarded-to-the-operator
  :invariant "an operator learns WHICH facet was missing"
  :file "src/payroll/governor.cljc"
  :find "             :taxlaw/out-of-scope (:taxlaw/out-of-scope withholding)"
  :replace "             :taxlaw/out-of-scope nil"}

 {:id :a-really-absent-jurisdiction-keeps-the-old-sentence
  :invariant "the new sentence must not replace the old one wholesale"
  :file "src/payroll/governor.cljc"
  :find "                       (str \"employer が法域 \" (pr-str juris)\n                            \" を宣言しているが kotoba.taxlaw に無い\""
  :replace "                       (str \"employer が法域 \" (pr-str juris)\n                            \" を宣言しているが検査できない\""}

 ;; --- 年末調整, 所得税法 第百九十条 (2026-08-18) -----------------------------
 ;;
 ;; taxlaw had read the article and NOTHING in this workspace called it. The
 ;; risk in acting on it is not that a run gets wrongly refused — the
 ;; assessment moves no money — but that the actor produces a NUMBER. The
 ;; year's correct tax comes from 別表 (税額表), which taxlaw records as
 ;; unread, so a figure here would arrive stamped with an article of the
 ;; Income Tax Act and nothing downstream could check it. Most of what
 ;; follows breaks a refusal and expects a test to notice.

 {:id :the-over-under-is-never-computed
  :invariant "第百九十条's over/under is not computable from anything read here"
  :file "src/payroll/nenmatsu.cljc"
  :find ":nenmatsu/over-or-under :not-computable"
  :replace ":nenmatsu/over-or-under (- withheld-recorded 0)"}

 {:id :the-years-tax-is-never-computed
  :invariant "and neither is the year's correct tax — 別表 was not read"
  :file "src/payroll/nenmatsu.cljc"
  :find ":nenmatsu/annual-tax :not-computable"
  :replace ":nenmatsu/annual-tax 0"}

 {:id :the-unread-table-is-named
  :invariant "the refusal names WHICH table nobody read, read off taxlaw"
  :file "src/payroll/nenmatsu.cljc"
  :find "   (:rule/amount-source-not-read\n    (taxlaw/facet-of jurisdiction :jurisdiction/wage-withholding))"
  :replace "   (:rule/no-such-key\n    (taxlaw/facet-of jurisdiction :jurisdiction/wage-withholding))"}

 {:id :the-recorded-sums-are-this-actors-own
  :invariant "wages recorded here are not 「その年中に…確定した給与等の金額」"
  :file "src/payroll/nenmatsu.cljc"
  :find ":nenmatsu/records-are-this-actors-only? true"
  :replace ":nenmatsu/records-are-this-actors-only? false"}

 {:id :the-ceiling-is-inclusive
  :invariant "二千万円以下 — at exactly 20,000,000 the employee is INSIDE"
  :file "src/payroll/nenmatsu.cljc"
  :find "(and (number? ceiling) (pos? run-count) (> wages ceiling)) :above-ceiling"
  :replace "(and (number? ceiling) (pos? run-count) (>= wages ceiling)) :above-ceiling"}

 {:id :the-ceiling-is-actually-read
  :invariant "the ceiling comes from taxlaw; a lookup that returns nothing must not silently stop checking"
  :file "src/payroll/nenmatsu.cljc"
  :find "ceiling (:rule/income-ceiling-yen (taxlaw/facet-of jurisdiction facet))"
  :replace "ceiling (:rule/no-such-ceiling (taxlaw/facet-of jurisdiction facet))"}

 {:id :under-the-recorded-ceiling-establishes-nothing
  :invariant "unseen wages only ADD, so `over` is certain and `under` is not"
  :file "src/payroll/nenmatsu.cljc"
  :find ":nenmatsu/establishes-inside? false"
  :replace ":nenmatsu/establishes-inside? true"}

 {:id :an-empty-record-is-not-zero-wages
  :invariant "no recorded runs is an empty record, never a fact about wages"
  :file "src/payroll/nenmatsu.cljc"
  :find ":no-runs-recorded? (zero? run-count)"
  :replace ":no-runs-recorded? false"}

 {:id :an-unobserved-declaration-is-not-an-unfiled-one
  :invariant "software cannot see a piece of paper; unseen is not `not filed`"
  :file "src/payroll/nenmatsu.cljc"
  :find "(nil? declaration) :declaration-not-observed"
  :replace "(nil? declaration) :declaration-not-filed"}

 {:id :a-string-is-not-a-declaration
  :invariant "`\"true\"` satisfies neither nil? nor false? and would fall through to :owed"
  :file "src/payroll/nenmatsu.cljc"
  :find "  (when (boolean? x) x))"
  :replace "  (when (some? x) x))"}

 {:id :not-yet-and-never-are-different-answers
  :invariant "`come back after the last payslip` is not `this employee does not qualify`"
  :file "src/payroll/nenmatsu.cljc"
  :find "(false? final?) :year-not-finished"
  :replace "(false? final?) :declaration-not-filed"}

 {:id :an-undeclared-jurisdiction-is-not-an-uncatalogued-one
  :invariant "`nobody said where` and `nobody read there` are different refusals"
  :file "src/payroll/nenmatsu.cljc"
  :find "(nil? jurisdiction) :jurisdiction-not-declared"
  :replace "(nil? :never) :jurisdiction-not-declared"}

 {:id :a-refusal-is-not-an-answer
  :invariant ":answerable? must not report an absence of an answer as one"
  :file "src/payroll/nenmatsu.cljc"
  :find ":nenmatsu/answerable? (contains? answers answer)"
  :replace ":nenmatsu/answerable? (some? answer)"}

 {:id :a-settlement-claim-is-not-a-verified-settlement
  :invariant "this actor cannot verify an amount it did not read a table for"
  :file "src/payroll/nenmatsu.cljc"
  :find "              :verified? false"
  :replace "              :verified? true"}

 {:id :an-assessment-record-is-not-a-payroll-run
  :invariant "counting one as wages would inflate the figure the ceiling tests"
  :file "src/payroll/nenmatsu.cljc"
  :find "(= :draft-payroll-run (:op r))"
  :replace "(some? (:op r))"}

 {:id :another-years-run-is-not-this-years-wages
